Generally, there are only four rules you need to consider when
wanting to fork, modify, edit or redistribute the software or other
licensed work put into this GitHub shitty repository.

- the `scams` directory is pretty much proprietary, because it may
  feature work that has been put publicly and is unlicensed OR 
  has been decompiled by someone I know and put here. if that's the case
  you may request deletion, preferably on eclairbakery's discord server
  which should be found somewhere in the `eclairbakery` GitHub organization
  (i'm too lazy to create this invite now and i don't want to know that
  it does not work after like 3 months), but keep in mind, that the file will
  be still available through commit history.

- if a project which is stored here has a `COPYING`, `LICENSE`, `LICENSE.md`,
  `docs/LICENSE.md` or anything similar, please refer to this file for license.

- you should NOT change this document although you are free to redistribute it 
  in other project and change it there 

- if case not clisted here, refer to the GPL-3.0-only license 
